# Docs index

This is a **navigator, not an authority**: it maps every doc with status and
audience. When the index and a target disagree, the target wins — fix the index.
Doctrine: `docs/rules/governance.md` "SSOT and the navigator index".

## Authority & precedence

When two docs overlap, precedence is:

1. `CLAUDE.md` — the repo binding (invariant, architecture, commands).
2. `docs/rules/*` — portable doctrine (governance, doc, python, skill, testing).
3. Module/app `README.md` — the owning context's public surface.
4. `docs/glossary/*` — ubiquitous language.
5. Everything else routes to one of the above.

